# Language Juggler

Capstone app for language learners to practice juggling multiple languages in one place.

## Status

Early exploration — core purpose and user value are still being defined. Prefer small, reversible changes until direction is settled.

## Stack

- **Frontend**: React (functional components, hooks)
- **Backend**: Node.js (when added)
- **Tooling**: npm, TypeScript preferred for new code

## Conventions

- Keep diffs minimal and focused; avoid over-engineering early prototypes
- Match existing patterns in the repo before introducing new abstractions
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, API keys); use `.env.example` for templates
- Update `README.md` when install steps or project status change materially
- Only create git commits when explicitly requested

## Product direction (draft)

Help learners switch between languages, retain vocabulary, and build confidence through practice — exact features TBD.
